<section>
  <h2>Build a list: loop to comprehension</h2>
  <code lang=python id=g1>
    <frame>
      def squares_of_evens(numbers):
          result = []
          for n in numbers:
              if n % 2 == 0:
                  result.append(n * n)
          return result
    </frame>
    <frame>
      def squares_of_evens(numbers):
          return [n * n for n in numbers if n % 2 == 0]
    </frame>
  </code>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>Lazily: generator expression</h2>
  <code lang=python id=g2>
    <frame>
      def total_of_squares(numbers):
          return sum([n * n for n in numbers if n % 2 == 0])
    </frame>
    <frame>
      def total_of_squares(numbers):
          return sum(n * n for n in numbers if n % 2 == 0)
    </frame>
  </code>
</section>

<notes>
  append in a loop -> list comprehension. Note how `if` moves inside.
</notes>
